The '''2025–26 Primera Federación''' season is the fifth for the [[Primera Federación]], the third-highest level in the [[Spanish football league system]]. Forty teams participate, divided into two groups of twenty clubs each based on geographical proximity. In each group, the champions are automatically promoted to [[Segunda División]] and the second to fifth placers will play promotion play-offs and the bottom five are relegated to the [[Segunda Federación]].

==Overview==
A total of 40 teams joined the league, including four relegated from the [[2024–25 Segunda División]], 26 retained from the [[2024–25 Primera Federación]], and ten promoted from the [[2024–25 Segunda Federación]]. [[Royal Spanish Football Federation|RFEF]] released the groups on 27 June 2025.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://rfef.es/es/noticias/aprobados-los-grupos-de-primera-federacion-para-la-temporada-202526|title=Aprobados los grupos de Primera Federación para la temporada 2025/26|trans-title=Approved the groups of Primera Federación for the 2025/26 season|publisher=[[Royal Spanish Football Federation|RFEF]]|language=es|date=27 June 2025|accessdate=27 June 2025}}</ref>

